Expose Field::oid() accessor so Drogon callers can read the PG column
OID without reaching into the private Result API. Result::oid() is
already a member of drogon::orm::Result; adding a public delegating
accessor on Field keeps the per-column OID reachable without a
consumer-side friendship on Row. Used by Plinth's 0.5.3 OID-driven
PG-type → JS-type mapping.

Upstreamable. Filed against drogonframework/drogon at ship.
---
 orm_lib/inc/drogon/orm/Field.h | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/orm_lib/inc/drogon/orm/Field.h b/orm_lib/inc/drogon/orm/Field.h
--- a/orm_lib/inc/drogon/orm/Field.h
+++ b/orm_lib/inc/drogon/orm/Field.h
@@ -49,6 +49,13 @@ class DROGON_EXPORT Field
     /// Column name
     const char *name() const;

+    /// Column type OID (PostgreSQL-specific; 0 for other backends).
+    /// Delegates to Result::oid, which is already friend-accessible.
+    int oid() const noexcept
+    {
+        return result_.oid(column_);
+    }
+
     /// Is this field's value null?
     bool isNull() const;

